# DNA-AND content · the visible universe as a whole: how big, how many galaxies, how they gather
# across-ly: the visible universe's width in light-years, as asked: 13.4 billion (the light-travel distance to the farthest
#   galaxies seen, such as GN-z11; measured as it is today, after space has stretched while the light travelled, the
#   visible universe is about 93 billion light-years across). The edge cannot be passed (for now).
# galaxies: how many galaxies it holds, about 100 billion (estimates run from 100 billion to 2 trillion).
# web-ly: the size of the cosmic web's cells (galaxies gather in walls and filaments round voids about 100 to 300 million
#   light-years across); web-contrast: how much denser the filaments are than the voids.
# region-ly: the regions galaxies are made in round you, a million light-years across; near-ly: how far round you galaxies are
#   made in full; glow-points: how many points show the rest of the universe's galaxies as a glow along the web.
# Spec: docs/CONTENT-FORMAT.md · content/galaxies.dnat

@universe visible
name: The visible universe
across-ly: 13.4e9
galaxies: 1e11
web-ly: 2e8
web-contrast: 6
region-ly: 1e6
near-ly: 8e6
glow-points: 300000
